---
// CAREERS — new page, 2026-09-07. The five open roles were the tail of /about, which is the wrong
// home: somebody looking for work does not read a company page to the bottom to find them, and
// their presence there pushed the actual company story down the page.
//
// Every role keeps its TRUE commitment shape in the meta line — equity, a single engagement, one
// consultation, a research partnership — because this is a pre-revenue, unfunded company and
// presenting a one-off consultation as a salaried post is the one claim on this page a reader
// could act on and be wrong about.
//
// Vocabulary updated in transit: "features" -> "applications", per the product reframe.
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import PageBanner from '../components/PageBanner.astro';
import Eyebrow from '../components/Eyebrow.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
import FormField from '../components/FormField.astro';

const roles = [
	{
		id: 'dataset-partner',
		title: 'Dataset partner',
		meta: 'Research partnership · no equity, no fee',
		flag: 'The binding constraint on everything else',
		lede: 'No clinical, biological, financial or defence data has ever touched this system.',
		body: [
			'Every result to date is CIFAR-10 or CIFAR-100. That is not a gap in the engineering — the engineering is done and published. It is a gap in access, and it is the single thing most limiting this company.',
			'If you hold a labelled dataset you suspect is dirty, or you have had a training run fail in a way nobody could explain afterwards, that is the conversation we want.',
			'A dataset is not a gift and we do not ask for one. It is a research partnership: we run the diagnostic, you receive the report, your data never leaves your environment unless you decide otherwise, and we publish together if you want to.',
		],
	},
	{
		id: 'co-founder',
		title: 'Co-founder',
		meta: 'Equity · full-time',
		flag: null,
		lede: 'The architecture exists. What is missing is a second person.',
		body: [
			'Someone who has stood on the other side of the buying table in one regulated domain — inside a hospital\'s AI group, a bank\'s model risk function, a biotech\'s data team, or coordinating a multi-site research consortium.',
			'Technically literate enough to survive a CTO\'s questions without needing to be the architect. What matters more is a network that cannot be built from where this is being built from.',
			'This is not a hire. It is the other half of the company, and it is described that way because pretending otherwise would waste a year of someone\'s life.',
		],
	},
	{
		id: 'researcher',
		title: 'Researcher',
		meta: 'Contract or equity · part-time to full-time',
		flag: null,
		lede: 'Four measurements decide how much of this is real, and not one has been run.',
		body: [
			'Two of them matter most. Does the per-component health signal actually lead the global loss curve, and by how much? And does inter-component disagreement separate mislabelled data from data that is merely hard?',
			'Four of the seven applications depend on the second answer. A negative result narrows what the product can be, which is exactly why the study is scheduled before the build rather than after it.',
			'Beyond those: the architecture is demonstrated on fully-connected, convolutional and residual families. Whether it generalises to transformers is genuinely open — not assumed and not dismissed.',
			'You would run experiments capable of falsifying the thesis, and co-author the result whichever way it goes.',
		],
	},
	{
		id: 'regulatory-consultant',
		title: 'Regulatory consultant',
		meta: 'One engagement · months of lead time',
		flag: null,
		lede: 'It gates the largest application in the product, and it has not started.',
		body: [
			'Someone who has actually filed a change-control plan for a machine learning system — under the FDA\'s PCCP framework, the EU AI Act, or an equivalent regime. Filed one, not read about one.',
			'The work is to read a specification and say whether the artefact format matches what a reviewer expects to receive, or whether it is something adjacent that a reviewer would not recognise.',
			'Either answer is worth having. If it is the wrong shape, that is worth knowing before more is built on it.',
		],
	},
	{
		id: 'data-protection-lawyer',
		title: 'Data-protection lawyer',
		meta: 'One consultation · no ongoing commitment',
		flag: null,
		lede: 'Until this is answered, certified deletion is a strong story rather than a certifiable product.',
		body: [
			'Someone working in AI data rights, willing to state what may and may not be put in writing when data is removed from a trained model.',
			'The specific question: if we delete a bounded structure trained on a named sample set, and we can state a measured bound on the residual influence of that data — what may we certify, what may our customer certify to theirs, and does any of it constitute erasure under Article 17?',
			'A certificate whose wording has not been checked is worse than no certificate, because it creates liability instead of removing it.',
		],
	},
];
---

<Page title="Careers" description={"Five roles ordered by how much each unblocks. The one that matters most is not a job — it is a partner who holds data under obligation."}>
	<PageBanner
		eyebrow="CAREERS"
		title="Five people would change what this company can do."
		trail={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Careers' }]}
	/>

	<section class="section container">
		<div class="car-intro">
			<div>
				<p class="car-lede">
					Oxiedo is pre-revenue and unfunded, and one person has built everything that exists. The
					commitment shape is stated on every role below — some are equity, one is a single
					consultation, one is a research partnership with no money attached in either direction —
					because it would be easy to make this list look larger than it is, and you would find
					out later.
				</p>
				<p class="car-lede">
					They are ordered by how much each one unblocks, not by seniority. The first is not a job
					at all, and it is the one that matters most.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="car-facts">
				<dl>
					<div><dt>Stage</dt><dd>Pre-revenue, pre-customer</dd></div>
					<div><dt>Team</dt><dd>One</dd></div>
					<div><dt>Location</dt><dd>Remote, with the headquarters relocating to San Francisco</dd></div>
					<div><dt>Reply time</dt><dd>A few days, usually less. Every message read by a person</dd></div>
				</dl>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section container reveal">
		<ol class="car-roles">
			{roles.map((r, i) => (
				<li class={`car-role${r.flag ? ' car-role--flag' : ''}`} id={r.id}>
					<div class="car-role-head">
						<span class="car-role-n tabular">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
						<div>
							<h2 class="car-role-title">{r.title}</h2>
							<p class="car-role-meta">{r.meta}</p>
							{r.flag && <p class="car-role-flag">{r.flag}</p>}
						</div>
					</div>
					<div class="car-role-body">
						<p class="car-role-lede">{r.lede}</p>
						{r.body.map((para) => <p>{para}</p>)}
						<Button variant="secondary" href="#apply" data-role={r.id}>Apply for this</Button>
					</div>
				</li>
			))}
		</ol>
	</section>

	<section class="band band--dark section reveal">
		<div class="container">
			<Eyebrow>HOW TO APPLY</Eyebrow>
			<h2 class="car-dark-title">There is no form, no tracking system and no process.</h2>
			<div class="car-apply">
				<p>
					Write to us and say which one, and what you have done that is relevant. A paragraph is
					enough. A CV is fine if you have one to hand, and not required if you do not.
				</p>
				<p>
					If it is not a fit we will say so directly rather than going quiet, because the
					alternative wastes your time and we would rather not. If it is, the next conversation is
					with the person who built this, because there is nobody else.
				</p>
			</div>
			<Button variant="primary" href="#apply">Apply</Button>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section container reveal" id="apply">
		<Eyebrow>APPLY</Eyebrow>
		<h2 class="car-apply-title">One form, and it goes straight to the founder.</h2>
		<p class="car-apply-lede">
			No tracking system, no automated screen, no acknowledgement email written by somebody else.
			If it is not a fit you will be told directly rather than left to work it out from silence.
		</p>

		<form class="car-form" id="apply-form" method="POST" action="/contact">
			<FormField
				id="apply-role"
				label="Which one?"
				options={[...roles.map((r) => r.title), 'Something else entirely']}
				required
			/>
			<FormField id="apply-name" label="Name" required />
			<FormField id="apply-email" label="Email" type="email" required />
			<FormField
				id="apply-links"
				label="Anything that shows your work"
				hint="A repository, a paper, a filing you wrote, a system you built. One good link beats a CV. Optional, but it is the part we read first."
			/>
			<FormField
				id="apply-why"
				label="Why this, and what would you want to own?"
				hint="Two honest paragraphs are worth more than a page of qualifications. If you are bringing data rather than looking for a job, say what you hold and what would have to be true for you to release it."
				multiline
				required
			/>
			<input type="hidden" name="intent" value="apply" />
			<div class="contact-form-honeypot" aria-hidden="true">
				<label for="apply-website">Website</label>
				<input type="text" id="apply-website" name="website" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" />
			</div>
			<Button variant="primary" type="submit">Send application</Button>
		</form>
	</section>

	<script>
		// A role card's "Apply for this" jumps to the form and preselects the role, so nobody has to
		// remember which of five they were reading. Progressive enhancement: with JS off the links
		// still land on the form, just without the preselection.
		function wireRoleLinks() {
			const select = document.getElementById('apply-role');
			if (!(select instanceof HTMLSelectElement)) return;
			document.querySelectorAll<HTMLAnchorElement>('a[data-role]').forEach((a) => {
				if (a.dataset.roleBound) return;
				a.dataset.roleBound = 'true';
				a.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
					e.preventDefault();
					const card = document.getElementById(a.dataset.role ?? '');
					const title = card?.querySelector('.car-role-title')?.textContent?.trim();
					if (title && Array.from(select.options).some((o) => o.value === title)) {
						select.value = title;
					}
					document.getElementById('apply')?.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' });
				});
			});
		}
		wireRoleLinks();
		document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', wireRoleLinks);
	</script>
</Page>
